Third-party software
====================

Ventoy
------
The app carries unmodified boot files of an official Ventoy release and
writes them to your USB drive. Ventoy is under the GNU General Public
License, version 3 or later, and contains other free software. Its notice,
license texts and source links are in third_party/ventoy/ and in the app.

libusb 1.0.26
-------------
Vendroid uses the libusb library, which is covered by the GNU Lesser General
Public License, version 2.1 or later. libusb is Copyright (C) its authors,
listed in the AUTHORS file of its source. The app ships libusb as separate
shared libraries built from unmodified source:

  https://github.com/libusb/libusb/tree/4239bc3a50014b8e6a5a2a59df1fff3b7469543b

The scripts in scripts/native/ of the Vendroid source rebuild these
libraries, so you can build a changed libusb and use it in the app.
License text: third_party/licenses/LGPL-2.1.txt

